{
  "bridge_text": "既然你已经听到了树干深处的秘密，那我们就推开那扇隐藏的门，看看莉娜接下来会遇见什么。",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "树洞里盘旋着一道向下的螺旋阶梯，最顶层的台阶上坐着一只穿着绿色补丁背心的老灰狐狸。他叫莫斯克，用像干枯落叶摩擦般的声音告诉莉娜，这棵树不是用来探险的，让她赶紧回家忘掉那阵嗡嗡声。莉娜却倔强地摇摇头，说她还没听见那嗡嗡声背后的真相，怎么能轻易忘记呢。"
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Even with his heart heavy from guarding the wood's deep secrets, the old fox watched Lina with a curious, flickering gaze. He seemed to wonder if she truly understood the weight of the magic hidden below.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Lina stood her ground, her eyes bright with a stubborn kindness that Mosk hadn't seen in many winters. Seeing her resolve, the fox sighed, his grumpy mask slipping just a fraction as he looked at the girl who refused to be frightened away by his stern words."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed toward the door, yet Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it on the step between them, offering it as a peace offering for the trouble of her arrival. Mosk stared at the crisp fruit for a long time, his stern posture softening, before he stood up and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "With Mosk watching her closely, Lina knew that simply turning back wasn't an option. She kept her gaze steady, waiting to see if the fox would accept her presence.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed toward the door, but Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season. She set it gently on the step between them. This is for the trouble of walking me down, she said. Mosk stared at the apple for a long time, his whiskers twitching. Finally, he stood up, straightened his patched green vest, and stepped onto the first stair without a word."
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom, the humming deepened into a soft, sorrowful song. A firefly the size of a robin lay on a bed of moss, her golden glow flickering like a dying candle. Mosk’s shoulders slumped. He whispered that she had been his friend once, and long ago, he had failed to bring her the medicine she needed. He had guarded the tree ever since, too ashamed to face the light."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s3"
