{
  "bridge_text": "The soft, green carpet beneath them seemed to hold its breath, waiting for the firefly's light to return. With the moss resting quiet and cool under their feet, Lina turned her attention back to the gentle queen.",
  "resume_strategy": "restart",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming was a quiet song, and a firefly the size of a robin lay on a bed of soft, velvety moss. Her glow was almost out. Mosk's whiskers trembled as he touched the damp green carpet. She had been his friend once, he whispered, and one winter long ago he had failed to bring her medicine in time. He had been guarding the tree ever since, ashamed to face her."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt and asked the firefly queen what she needed. A drop of warm milk and a kind word, said the queen, that was all medicine ever was. Mosk fetched the milk in a thimble and laid his paw beside hers. The queen's glow steadied, casting a golden light over the mossy floor. The humming inside the tree turned into a tune Lina had not heard before, and Mosk, for the first time in years, hummed along."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
